    {
      "object": "block",
      "id": "2ada6e41-f23e-80fe-b9da-c1ef58661021",
      "parent": {
        "type": "page_id",
        "page_id": "2ada6e41-f23e-80d0-8119-e9f63ddc2377"
      },
      "created_time": "2025-11-16T19:12:00.000Z",
      "last_edited_time": "2025-11-16T21:19:00.000Z",
      "created_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "last_edited_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "has_children": false,
      "in_trash": false,
      "type": "bulleted_list_item",
      "bulleted_list_item": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "Sometimes, it feels like I/Manifund are just chasing the shadow of the Future Fund. There was this amazing group of folks, helping direct unprecedented amounts of money towards their best conception of “good”. The Future Fund was best example of what I would like Manifund to be. But I don’t think we’ve had anywhere near that impact — was it just for a lack of committed funders? Skill issue, on my part? I don’t know.",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "Sometimes, it feels like I/Manifund are just chasing the shadow of the Future Fund. There was this amazing group of folks, helping direct unprecedented amounts of money towards their best conception of “good”. The Future Fund was best example of what I would like Manifund to be. But I don’t think we’ve had anywhere near that impact — was it just for a lack of committed funders? Skill issue, on my part? I don’t know.",
            "href": null
          }
        ],
        "color": "default"
      }
    },
    {
      "object": "block",
      "id": "2ada6e41-f23e-8027-82ff-c91c7feae11b",
      "parent": {
        "type": "page_id",
        "page_id": "2ada6e41-f23e-80d0-8119-e9f63ddc2377"
      },
      "created_time": "2025-11-16T19:14:00.000Z",
      "last_edited_time": "2025-11-16T21:00:00.000Z",
      "created_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "last_edited_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "has_children": false,
      "in_trash": false,
      "type": "bulleted_list_item",
      "bulleted_list_item": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "People sure seem eager to forget their connection to the Future Fund. This is understandable given the FTX fallout, but also makes me sad. Grantees don’t talk about the windfalls they received; beneficiaries of funded programs either don’t know or don’t talk about the good that the money accomplished; regrantors don’t speak about their experience directing funding. Even the Future Fund’s employees — their bios either vaguely refer to it eg “did grantmaking in AI safety and biosecurity”, or skip the mention altogether. ",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "People sure seem eager to forget their connection to the Future Fund. This is understandable given the FTX fallout, but also makes me sad. Grantees don’t talk about the windfalls they received; beneficiaries of funded programs either don’t know or don’t talk about the good that the money accomplished; regrantors don’t speak about their experience directing funding. Even the Future Fund’s employees — their bios either vaguely refer to it eg “did grantmaking in AI safety and biosecurity”, or skip the mention altogether. ",
            "href": null
          }
        ],
        "color": "default"
      }
    },
    {
      "object": "block",
      "id": "2ada6e41-f23e-8098-988a-f14152e62ac9",
      "parent": {
        "type": "page_id",
        "page_id": "2ada6e41-f23e-80d0-8119-e9f63ddc2377"
      },
      "created_time": "2025-11-16T19:12:00.000Z",
      "last_edited_time": "2025-11-16T21:19:00.000Z",
      "created_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "last_edited_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "has_children": false,
      "in_trash": false,
      "type": "bulleted_list_item",
      "bulleted_list_item": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "There was a while where people associated with FTX or the Future Fund had a hard time finding their next job. For example, my housemate Joel Becker (who’d worked on FTX Foundation, associated but not the same as the Future Fund) had job offers fall through due to orgs being scared of PR risk. This seemed like a terrible outcome to me — basically, we were sidelining EA’s best and brightest. I think almost all of them have now landed on their feet (eg Joel’s ",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "There was a while where people associated with FTX or the Future Fund had a hard time finding their next job. For example, my housemate Joel Becker (who’d worked on FTX Foundation, associated but not the same as the Future Fund) had job offers fall through due to orgs being scared of PR risk. This seemed like a terrible outcome to me — basically, we were sidelining EA’s best and brightest. I think almost all of them have now landed on their feet (eg Joel’s ",
            "href": null
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "killing it at METR",
              "link": {
                "url": "https://metr.org/blog/2025-07-10-early-2025-ai-experienced-os-dev-study/"
              }
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "killing it at METR",
            "href": "https://metr.org/blog/2025-07-10-early-2025-ai-experienced-os-dev-study/"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "), but I still consider that period to have been a major blunder of us as a movement.",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "), but I still consider that period to have been a major blunder of us as a movement.",
            "href": null
          }
        ],
        "color": "default"
      }
    },
    {
      "object": "block",
      "id": "2ada6e41-f23e-80f6-af63-e80432ff48ee",
      "parent": {
        "type": "page_id",
        "page_id": "2ada6e41-f23e-80d0-8119-e9f63ddc2377"
      },
      "created_time": "2025-11-16T19:24:00.000Z",
      "last_edited_time": "2025-11-16T21:19:00.000Z",
      "created_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "last_edited_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "has_children": false,
      "in_trash": false,
      "type": "bulleted_list_item",
      "bulleted_list_item": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "One unfortunate legacy of the Future Fund is the bankruptcy and clawback proceedings. Manifund and Manifold are still in the process of settling things with the FTX estate ourselves — pretty frustrating, given how they already have all the funds to make creditors whole. The best analogy I have for the difference between the Future Fund we worked with vs the estate we’re dealing with now, is having dear friend go through a psychotic break and then subsequently turn on you.",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "One unfortunate legacy of the Future Fund is the bankruptcy and clawback proceedings. Manifund and Manifold are still in the process of settling things with the FTX estate ourselves — pretty frustrating, given how they already have all the funds to make creditors whole. The best analogy I have for the difference between the Future Fund we worked with vs the estate we’re dealing with now, is having dear friend go through a psychotic break and then subsequently turn on you.",
            "href": null
          }
        ],
        "color": "default"
      }
    },
    {
      "object": "block",
      "id": "2ada6e41-f23e-8073-a5d6-d405ed429d93",
      "parent": {
        "type": "page_id",
        "page_id": "2ada6e41-f23e-80d0-8119-e9f63ddc2377"
      },
      "created_time": "2025-11-16T19:34:00.000Z",
      "last_edited_time": "2025-11-16T21:00:00.000Z",
      "created_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "last_edited_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "has_children": false,
      "in_trash": false,
      "type": "bulleted_list_item",
      "bulleted_list_item": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "I’m quite nostalgic about “FTX summer”, the 2022 period when we as a community were proud to be EA; to care about AI safety; to loudly, transparently, stand for our beliefs. Now, “EA” is a dirty word, with former leaders distancing themselves from the term, OpenPhil taking the phrase out of their programs. People who were inspired by its tenets and took roles organizing, now hide their affiliations to get jobs in politics or tech. And rationalist leaders and EA funders have gone through a messy public divorce.",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "I’m quite nostalgic about “FTX summer”, the 2022 period when we as a community were proud to be EA; to care about AI safety; to loudly, transparently, stand for our beliefs. Now, “EA” is a dirty word, with former leaders distancing themselves from the term, OpenPhil taking the phrase out of their programs. People who were inspired by its tenets and took roles organizing, now hide their affiliations to get jobs in politics or tech. And rationalist leaders and EA funders have gone through a messy public divorce.",
            "href": null
          }
        ],
        "color": "default"
      }
    },
    {
      "object": "block",
      "id": "2ada6e41-f23e-805e-a7b5-ffda9491663f",
      "parent": {
        "type": "page_id",
        "page_id": "2ada6e41-f23e-80d0-8119-e9f63ddc2377"
      },
      "created_time": "2025-11-16T21:20:00.000Z",
      "last_edited_time": "2025-11-16T21:23:00.000Z",
      "created_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "last_edited_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "has_children": false,
      "in_trash": false,
      "type": "bulleted_list_item",
      "bulleted_list_item": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "At the time, the EA community complained somewhat about the optics of freely spending, of large flows of money entering the space. I thought, and mostly think, that these concerns are overblown, and to a first order approximation, more money = good. I also think it’s relevant that, after a relative period of drought, we should soon be entering a phase with large amounts of money available for EA — from Anthropic employees, and other folks waking up to the dangers of AI.",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "At the time, the EA community complained somewhat about the optics of freely spending, of large flows of money entering the space. I thought, and mostly think, that these concerns are overblown, and to a first order approximation, more money = good. I also think it’s relevant that, after a relative period of drought, we should soon be entering a phase with large amounts of money available for EA — from Anthropic employees, and other folks waking up to the dangers of AI.",
            "href": null
          }
        ],
        "color": "default"
      }
    },
